# Capture composition SSOT lock (Customer / financial-main)

## Proven classification — MK-260925-002

**C. CAPTURE_USES_CUSTOMER_PAYABLE_ONLY** (primary)

First broken assignment (pre-SSOT `revolutCompletionCapture`):

```
finalFarePence = computeCaptureAmount(...).capture_amount_pence
// = final_fare_pence + tips_pence   ← no receivable
```

Then `planRevolutCompletionCapture` set `release_remainder_pence = hold − finalFare`,
so the 36p RESERVED debt was treated as unused hold remainder. Metadata still had
`customer_receivables_pence` (not D). Buffer field was not rewritten as 36 (A not
proven as a buffer-field write); collapse was via capture-payable-only + remainder.

Co-fact **B**: receivable component dropped before capture POST.

## Canonical typed components (never infer across types)

1. `trip_fare_component_pence`
2. `preauth_buffer_component_pence` — explicit persisted buffer only
3. `customer_receivable_component_pence` — same-session RESERVED only
4. `tip_component_pence`

```
displayed = fare + receivable
auth_target = fare + receivable + buffer
capture_target = fare + tip + receivable
release = auth_target − capture_target   // buffer when tip=0; NEVER receivable
```

## Never remove

- `planCaptureComposition` / `planTypedMoneyTargets` / `rejectAuthorisationRemainderAsBuffer`
- Persist composition before provider POST
- Settle only from planned receivable component
- Tip auth decline must not fare-capture

## Lock tests

`supabase/tests/_shared/captureCompositionSSOTLock.test.ts`

**If they fail, fix the code — never delete or soften the lock.**

## Do not

- Derive buffer as `authorised − fare`
- Derive receivable from authorisation remainder
- POST `customer_payable` alone when RESERVED exist
- Put receivable into TEN / commission / tip / payout
- Enable `CUSTOMER_RECEIVABLE_FOLD_ENABLED` in this PR
